---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="I Started Building It Before I Knew Their Name."
  description="The wild part about the Barstool Sports production at Shear Media Studios is that I started designing for it long before Barstool ever gave me the chance to bid. I just didn't know it was Barstool yet."
  image="/images/studios/Shear-Media-Studios-Control-Room.jpg"
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "I Started Building It Before I Knew Their Name.",
    "description": "The wild part about the Barstool Sports production at Shear Media Studios is that I started designing for it long before Barstool ever gave me the chance to bid.",
    "datePublished": "2026-09-12",
    "image": "https://www.peteguzzo.com/images/studios/Shear-Media-Studios-Control-Room.jpg",
    "url": "https://www.peteguzzo.com/industry-insights/barstool-sports-shear-media-studios-tampa",
    "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Pete Guzzo", "url": "https://www.peteguzzo.com" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Pete Guzzo", "url": "https://www.peteguzzo.com" }
  })} />

  <style>
    .bs-eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #8a8784;
    }
    .bs-section {
      border-top: 1px solid #e8e6e3;
      padding-block: 5rem;
    }
    .bs-h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-serif);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      line-height: 1.15;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      color: #161513;
      margin-top: 0.75rem;
      margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
    }
    .bs-body {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: #38352f;
      max-width: 38rem;
    }
    .bs-body p {
      margin-bottom: 1.5em;
    }
    .bs-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .bs-punch {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1;
      color: #555250;
      max-width: 38rem;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1.1rem;
      margin-block: 2rem;
    }

    /* Large callout / thesis statements */
    .bs-callout {
      font-family: var(--font-serif);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
      line-height: 1.35;
      letter-spacing: -0.015em;
      color: #161513;
      max-width: 34rem;
      margin-block: 2.25rem;
    }
    .bs-callout.rust { color: #b5482b; }

    .bs-quote {
      font-family: var(--font-serif);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.4rem);
      line-height: 1.45;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: #161513;
      border-left: 3px solid #b5482b;
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
      margin-block: 2rem;
      max-width: 34rem;
    }

    .bs-meta {
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      color: #9a9794;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .bs-meta a { color: #b5482b; }

    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .bs-body { color: #c8c4be; }
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .bs-punch { color: #9e9a95; }
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .bs-h2,
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .bs-callout,
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .bs-quote { color: #faf9f6; }
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .bs-callout.rust { color: #b5482b; }
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .bs-eyebrow,
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .bs-meta { color: #6e6b68; }
      :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .bs-section { border-top-color: #2e2c2a; }
    }
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .bs-body { color: #c8c4be; }
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .bs-punch { color: #9e9a95; }
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .bs-h2,
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .bs-callout,
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .bs-quote { color: #faf9f6; }
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .bs-callout.rust { color: #b5482b; }
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .bs-eyebrow,
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .bs-meta { color: #6e6b68; }
    :root[data-theme="dark"] .bs-section { border-top-color: #2e2c2a; }
  </style>

  <article>

    <!-- ─── HERO ─── -->
    <section style="padding-block: 3rem 5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #e8e6e3;">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
        <a href="/industry-insights" class="bs-meta" style="display:inline-block; margin-bottom: 2rem;">← Back to Industry Insights</a>
        <div class="bs-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">Studio Systems &nbsp;·&nbsp; September 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Pete Guzzo</div>
        <h1 class="font-display" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.5rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.025em; max-width: 30rem; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
          I Started Building It Before I Knew Their Name.
        </h1>
        <div class="bs-body">
          <p>The wild part about the Barstool Sports production at Shear Media Studios is that I started designing for it long before Barstool ever gave me the chance to bid.</p>
          <p>I just didn't know it was Barstool yet.</p>
          <p>Around mid-August, I was sitting across from a friend and industry colleague in his studio business center. We were talking shop, comparing jobs, talking production.</p>
          <p>He looked at me and said, almost curiously:</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-quote">"How the hell did you get Barstool Sports?"</div>

        <div class="bs-punch" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
          <span>I kind of grinned.</span>
          <span>Yeah.</span>
          <span>That was pretty cool.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-body" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
          <p>Then he started doing what people in this business do. Friends, colleagues, competitors, frienemies — whatever you want to call us.</p>
          <p>He started asking questions.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>How did you land it?</span>
          <span>How are you running it?</span>
          <span>How did you build the workflow?</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-body">
          <p>And honestly, my answer was pretty simple.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-callout">I started planning for it a long time ago.</div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>Not Barstool specifically.</span>
          <span>A production like Barstool.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-body" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
          <p>I wanted a studio operation that could handle a nimble podcaster or content creator one day, a national commercial the next, and then a recurring five-camera live broadcast without having to reinvent the entire building every time somebody new walked through the door.</p>
          <p>And I wanted Plan B, C and D sitting behind Plan A.</p>
          <p>I knew if I put this piece over here, that piece over there, connected the control room, network, studios, people and technology correctly, eventually it would become a pretty big sandbox for people to play in.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>But somebody still had to put the sandbox together.</span>
          <span>That was my job.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── IT WAS NEVER JUST THE ROOM ─── -->
    <section class="bs-section">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bs-eyebrow">Strategy</div>
        <h2 class="bs-h2">It Was Never Just the Room.</h2>

        <div class="bs-body">
          <p>I helped design and strategize the studio around where I thought production was going, not just what clients were asking for that day.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>Podcasting.</span>
          <span>Creator content.</span>
          <span>Commercial production.</span>
          <span>Episodic work.</span>
          <span>Live television.</span>
          <span>eSports.</span>
          <span>Remote production.</span>
          <span>Broadcast contribution without relying on traditional satellite workflows.</span>
          <span>SRT.</span>
          <span>A control room capable of talking to another control room hundreds of miles away.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-body">
          <p>And then I had to market it and sell it.</p>
          <p>Because I don't believe in:</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-callout rust">Build it and they will come.</div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>You design it.</span>
          <span>Strategize it.</span>
          <span>Build it.</span>
          <span>Then make sure the right people understand what you built and why they need it.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-body" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
          <p>Eventually, Barstool showed up.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>Five cameras.</span>
          <span>Custom set.</span>
          <span>Weekly live production.</span>
          <span>Remote line cut.</span>
          <span>Signals moving between Tampa Bay and a broadcast operation in another city in real time.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>Exactly the kind of production I had been thinking about.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>So I sold it.</span>
          <span>Then we had to make the damn thing work.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── FIVE ENGINEERS WERE WAITING ─── -->
    <section class="bs-section">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bs-eyebrow">The Transmission Test</div>
        <h2 class="bs-h2">Five Engineers Were Waiting.</h2>

        <div class="bs-body">
          <p>Before the first show, we hit a network problem.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>No static IP.</span>
          <span>Port forwarding.</span>
          <span>Routing.</span>
          <span>SRT.</span>
          <span>Transmission paths.</span>
          <span>Five engineers waiting on the other side for the test to clear.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>I'm not a network engineer.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-callout">I'm the guy who sold the production and needed the network to work.</div>

        <div class="bs-body">
          <p>Fortunately, months earlier, I had started building my AI agents and CORTEX for exactly this kind of situation.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>Not this exact problem.</span>
          <span>That's the point.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-body" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
          <p>I was training the agents to handle the <em>class</em> of problem — no static IP, port forwarding, routing camera signals out of your building and into a broadcast ingest somewhere else. The kind of IT and network problem that stops a production in its tracks because the person who sold the show isn't a network engineer and the network engineers are waiting on the other end of a test call.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>I was teaching them to do reconnaissance first.</span>
          <span>Read the documentation.</span>
          <span>Understand the environment.</span>
          <span>Figure out what matters.</span>
          <span>Then solve.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-body" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
          <p>So I paired those agents with Codex, dug through our network architecture, worked through the routing and transmission path, and learned what I needed in real time.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>The signal connected.</span>
          <span>The test cleared.</span>
          <span>The show went live.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── TECHNOLOGY WAS ONLY HALF ─── -->
    <section class="bs-section">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bs-eyebrow">The Team</div>
        <h2 class="bs-h2">But Technology Was Only Half of It.</h2>

        <div class="bs-body">
          <p>A great system with the wrong people is still a bad system.</p>
          <p>I also had to build the team around it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>Seasoned veterans.</span>
          <span>Younger crew members.</span>
          <span>People who knew broadcast.</span>
          <span>People still learning it.</span>
          <span>People who could work inside a recurring production without everything becoming dependent on one person knowing every answer.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>That matters.</span>
          <span>Because a recurring production can't run on heroics every week.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>The workflow has to be teachable.</span>
          <span>Repeatable.</span>
          <span>Everybody has to know where they fit.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-body" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
          <p>And if somebody new comes in, the operation has to be strong enough to bring them up to speed.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>That's the real sandbox.</span>
          <span>Not just cameras and control rooms.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-callout">People, technology and systems all working together.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── THEN IT ALL CAME BACK AROUND ─── -->
    <section class="bs-section">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bs-eyebrow">The Point</div>
        <h2 class="bs-h2">Then It All Came Back Around.</h2>

        <div class="bs-body">
          <p>Sitting across from my friend that day, I realized the answer to his question wasn't really:</p>
          <p>"How did you get Barstool?"</p>
          <p>It was:</p>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-callout" style="font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.5vw, 2rem);">
          I had been preparing for a Barstool before I knew Barstool was coming.
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>I designed the studio before I knew the client.</span>
          <span>Built the sales strategy before I knew the opportunity.</span>
          <span>Developed the AI agents before I knew the technical problem.</span>
          <span>Built the team before I knew exactly what production would test them.</span>
          <span>Then one day all of it met in the same room.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-punch" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
          <span>That's how I work.</span>
          <span>I don't design for one client.</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bs-callout rust">I design so the right client can happen.</div>

        <div class="bs-punch">
          <span>Build the capability.</span>
          <span>Build the team.</span>
          <span>Sell it.</span>
          <span>Solve what nobody anticipated.</span>
          <span>Then make sure the damn thing works.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── FOOTER NOTE ─── -->
    <section class="bs-section" style="padding-block: 3rem;">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
        <p class="bs-meta" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
          Shear Media Studios is an approximately 15,000 sq. ft. multi-studio facility in St. Petersburg, FL — soundstages, podcast and influencer suites, a live-commerce environment, and a full broadcast control room. <a href="https://shearmediastudios.com" style="color: var(--color-rust);">shearmediastudios.com</a>
        </p>
        <a href="/industry-insights" class="bs-meta" style="display:inline-block;">← Back to Industry Insights</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </article>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section style="background: var(--color-ink); color: var(--color-paper);">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display" style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); max-width: 32rem; margin-inline: auto; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
        Got something tangled up that needs a hand?
      </h2>
      <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
        <a href="/contact" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 1rem 2rem; border-radius: 9999px; font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 500; background: var(--color-paper); color: var(--color-ink); text-decoration: none;">
          Let's Talk
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
